    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This three-bedroom semi-detached residence offers an excellent opportunity for purchasers seeking a home with plenty of potential. While the property would benefit from refurbishment and modernisation throughout, it provides well-proportioned accommodation and gives the new owner an ideal opportunity to create a home to their own taste.\n\nThe ground floor accommodation comprises an entrance hall, spacious living room with fireplace, and an open-plan kitchen/dining area with access to the rear garden.\n\nUpstairs there are three bedrooms, a family bathroom, landing, hot press and useful additional storage.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from a front garden with off-street parking, while to the rear is an enclosed garden laid mainly in lawn with a garden shed and side access.\nWith its good accommodation, established location and considerable scope for improvement, No. 101 represents an attractive opportunity for first-time buyers, investors or anyone looking for a property they can refurbish and make their own.\n\nKilcarn Court was built in 1985 and is located on the south side of Navan, just off the Dublin Road and adjacent to the Ardboyne Hotel and Navan Rugby and Tennis Clubs. Navan Town Centre is within walking distance. Local amenities include Our Lady`s Hospital, Solstice Arts Centre and Meath County Library, Navan and Johnstown shopping centres and several primary and secondary schools.\n\nViewing is highly recommended!\n\nGROUND FLOOR\n\nEntrance Hall: 1.83m x 4.06m\nWith staircase to first floor\n\nLiving Room: 3.29m x 5.56m\nSpacious living room with large front window providing plenty of natural light and feature brick fireplace.\n\nDining Area: 3.17m x 4.79m\nGenerous dining/family area adjoining the kitchen with access to the rear garden.\n\nKitchen: 2.48m x 3.29m\nFitted kitchen with wall and floor units, worktop space and tiled splashback. Open-plan connection to the dining area.\n\nFIRST FLOOR\n\nLanding: 2.05m x 3.34m\nWith hot press\n\nBedroom 1: 3.08m x 4.23m\nGenerous front double bedroom\n\nBedroom 2: 3.08m x 3.71m\nSpacious double bedroom, overlooking the rear garden\n\nBedroom 3: 2.45m x 3.09m\nGood-sized front bedroom\n\nBathroom: 2.05m x 2.31m\nFamily bathroom with window.\n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
